WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.529
I’m just gonna come right out and say it:
Zac Efron, you stole my career sir!

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:07.169
It should’ve been me as Troy Bolton in High School
Musical.

00:00:07.169 --> 00:00:12.490
We both dance, act, and sing...except one
of us doesn’t need autotune *cough cough*

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:17.980
who performed as kids, we were born less than
a year apart, and we can rock the short and

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:18.980
the long hairstyles.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.000
And look at that steely gaze!

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.340
We are EXACTLY the same!

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.420
We are MOSTLY the same!

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:48.020
Hello internet, welcome to Film Theory, the
show that encourages viewers to getcha, getcha,

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.440
getcha, getcha head in the game, if the game
is reinterpreting beloved franchises.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.519
If you’re not onto it by now, you probably
don’t even Disney Channel original movie,

00:00:57.519 --> 00:01:00.469
bro, because today’s episode is all about
High School Musical.

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:05.760
That’s right, here on Film Theory, we only
tackle the freshest, hottest movie series

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.840
that haven’t had an installment in nearly
a decade (unless you count Sharpay’s Fabulous

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.350
Adventure, which I obviously do).

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:16.320
When I was still acting in theater, I was
in a big regional production of High School

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.000
Musical as Troy’s understudy, and that gave
me plenty of time to overthink the plot.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.480
Inbetween bouts of icing our vocal chords.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:27.480
I mean this kind of thing was my life when
I was a teenager: musicals, theater, show

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:28.480
choir.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.470
You name it, if there was a chance to perform
onstage and not have to interact with popular

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.650
people, well boy howdy was I involved.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:39.100
And after spending so much time studying the
show, I’ve ALWAYS had a bone to pick with

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.100
HSM.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:44.140
Well, a few bones to pick because there’s
no way Juilliard is really going to send acting

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:49.280
scouts to a random public high school in Albuquerque
to watch a show written by a student.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:55.700
Anyway, the movies bend over backwards trying
to convince you that Sharpay, the quote-unquote

00:01:55.710 --> 00:02:00.230
spoiled, rich, theater diva is the villain
of the story...but she’s NOT.

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:06.200
In fact, when you stop and actually look at
the series, Sharpay is the ONLY one with redeemable

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.200
qualities.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.939
You hear that Vanessa Hudgens and Zac Efron!

00:02:08.939 --> 00:02:11.730
Your empire of fame is built on LIES!

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:12.830
Lies I say!

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:15.110
Think it’s just a chip on my shoulder?

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:18.379
Well let’s look at the evidence and “Bop-bop-bop,
bop to the” bottom of this case.

00:02:18.379 --> 00:02:22.390
Now in case you need a cram session before
this High School Musical final exam, here

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:23.489
it is in a nutshell.

00:02:23.489 --> 00:02:27.850
In the original High School Musical, our heroes
Gabriella and Troy meet when they do karaoke

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:31.720
together at a New Year’s Eve party, conveniently
finding out shortly thereafter that Gabriella

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.420
is transferring to Troy’s school.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:38.310
She’s a science nerd who wants to find a
new place for herself at this school, and

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:41.879
he’s a star basketball player who wants
to find a new place for himself in Gabriella’s

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:42.879
pants.

00:02:42.879 --> 00:02:47.889
On a whim, they decide to audition for the
high school musical...oh I get the title now!

00:02:47.889 --> 00:02:51.940
Even though they’re rejected for being too
late and don’t prepare anything, they get

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.499
a callback for the lead roles.

00:02:53.499 --> 00:02:57.290
This doesn’t sit well with Sharpay and her
twin brother Ryan, who are the diehard members

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.970
of the drama club...which, now that I’m
writing it out, when the villain of your movie

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:05.040
is supposedly a THEATER KID, you should already
be asking questions.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:05.680
Oh no!

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.480
They’re going to shame me with their BOX
STEPS!

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.480
Don't you do that in my direction!

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.540
Oh they're pulling out the viewpoints! She's commenting on my stance!

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.540
Sorry the theater kid is coming rushing back to me!

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.200
Anyway, Sharpay and Ryan convince the drama
teacher to move the callbacks to the same

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:24.370
day as Troy’s basketball championship and
Gabriella’s scholastic decathlon.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:29.249
Troy and Gabriella’s other friends think
they should choose between the activities

00:03:29.249 --> 00:03:34.080
they’ve already committed to or this musical,
but NAH, they’re the hot protagonists in

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.930
a made-for-TV Disney movie, so they don’t
and Troy and Gabriella win everything, including

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:41.180
the leads in the musical, the decathalon,
and the last shot of the basketball game.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.820
Wow, growing up is so difficult when you're young and beautiful.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.260
High School Musical 2 is pretty much the same
thing but over the summer and with a country

00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:51.520
club talent show instead of a musical, and
High School Musical 3 is pretty much the same

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:54.180
thing as HSM 1 but now they’re seniors and focused
on college.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:55.180
Got it?

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.180
Good.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:57.180
So what makes Sharpay the villain?

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:00.730
Well, ask anyone who knows these movies, and
their arguments fall into one of three camps:

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:05.329
1) She’s a diva who won’t share the spotlight;
2) She’s trying to steal Troy away from

00:04:05.329 --> 00:04:09.849
Gabriella; and 3) She’s a spoiled rich girl
who expects everything to be handed to her.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:14.719
That’s what these movies want you to believe,
but if you actually stop and objectively look

00:04:14.719 --> 00:04:20.340
at her actions across these cinematic masterpieces,
you see that this couldn’t be further from

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:21.389
the truth.

00:04:21.389 --> 00:04:24.930
Complaint #1: Sharpay is a diva who won’t
share the spotlight.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:28.900
Very early in the first High School Musical,
we establish that Sharpay is super mean.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:32.340
Just look at this conversation: “Oh, were you
going to sign up, too?

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:35.509
My brother and I have starred in all the school’s
productions, and we really welcome newcomers.

00:04:35.509 --> 00:04:38.060
There are a lot of supporting roles in the
show.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:39.759
I’m sure we can find something for you.”

00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:43.509
Okay, there’s definitely a tone issue, but
let’s think about what she’s actually

00:04:43.509 --> 00:04:44.509
saying.

00:04:44.509 --> 00:04:47.940
She isn’t discouraging the pretty new girl
from auditioning -- in fact, she even says

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:52.340
that they WELCOME new people into the club,
going so far as to say there are lots of roles,

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:57.180
so she’d be likely to get in even if Gabriella’s
a complete newb to performing on stage...which,

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.160
let’s not forget, SHE ABSOLUTELY IS.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:04.879
This girl is so inexperienced she freezes
up at the freaking audition: “I can’t

00:05:04.879 --> 00:05:05.879
do it, Troy.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.160
Not with all these people staring at me.”

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.140
Oh you can't do it can ya?

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.840
Well, it’s not like people are going
to be staring at you if you’re the lead

00:05:10.841 --> 00:05:12.729
character in a musical or anything?

00:05:12.729 --> 00:05:16.980
Sharpay is definitely full of herself to assume
she’ll be the lead, but then again, no one

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.300
else signs up to audition FOR the lead.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.040
We see the sign up sheet.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:24.340
And even if they did, look at the other talent
she’s had to go up against!

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:39.300
East High... Not quite the strongest arts program.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:43.419
And yes, at first, it might seem underhanded
that she convinces Ms. Darbus the theater

00:05:43.419 --> 00:05:47.040
teacher to change the callbacks to the same
day as the basketball game, but Sharpay is

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.539
just testing Gabriella and Troy’s resolve
to see if they’d really be committed to

00:05:50.539 --> 00:05:51.539
the show.

00:05:51.539 --> 00:05:56.830
Because let’s face it, Gabriella and Troy
have other activities, other friends, and

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:01.080
each other; what else does Sharpay have besides
theater and a brother who wears stupid hats?

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:05.639
Now, the idea of testing their commitment
may seem absurd, but her fears are well-founded:

00:06:05.639 --> 00:06:10.960
In High School Musical 3, Troy actively ditches
out of the first act of his senior show so

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:14.340
he can drive to visit Gabriella when she’s
away at another school.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.360
Troy Bolton just sent me a text.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:18.040
‘Been driving all night.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:20.020
I’ll try and get there for the second act.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.400
Break a leg’ Break a leg?

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.680
What does that mean?

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:25.560
Dude, I think it’s showbiz for ‘you’re
going on’.”

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:29.759
“Yeah guys, sorry for completely trashing
the months of work we put into this thing...I

00:06:29.759 --> 00:06:31.720
had to go make out with my girlfriend.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:35.120
Don’t worry, I’ll be there to grace the
show with my six-pack abs in the second act”

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:38.919
But let’s not forget, a true diva would
rather not be a part of the show at all instead

00:06:38.919 --> 00:06:40.940
of playing second fiddle to someone else.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:45.780
Well in NONE of the High School Musical movies
does Sharpay get the glory, but she comes

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.669
around in all three!

00:06:47.669 --> 00:06:51.469
After Gabriella gets the lead in High School
Musical, Sharpay is cast as her understudy

00:06:51.469 --> 00:06:54.100
but still congratulates her and tells her
to break a leg.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:59.260
"Well congratulations... I guess I'm going to be the understudy in case you can't make one of the shows, so break a leg."

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:03.919
And we find out in the beginning of HSM 2
that Sharpay even gave Gabriella vocal exercises

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:05.300
that helped her in the role.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:10.320
"Sharpay we got off to a rough start, but you really came through. I mean you helped me with the winter musical.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.740
Those vocal exercises..."

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:16.180
That’s...surprisingly gracious for someone
who is supposedly so egotistical.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:20.810
Now look at the end of that movie: Sharpay
and Troy are slated to sing together at the

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:22.340
country club’s talent show.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:28.310
Her brother Ryan and his stupid, STUPID hat betrays
his sister by giving Troy a new song to sing

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:34.160
with Gabriella so that Sharpay can’t participate
in the one thing she was hoping for the entire

00:07:34.169 --> 00:07:35.919
summer. So what did she do?

00:07:35.919 --> 00:07:39.699
Instead of making a scene or wrecking the
show, Sharpay recovers, chooses to sing as

00:07:39.699 --> 00:07:45.020
part of the group, wins the Star Dazzle Award
as best performer, then GRACIOUSLY gives the

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:48.569
award to the brother who just stabbed her
in the back!

00:07:48.569 --> 00:07:55.240
“And this year’s Star Dazzle goes to...of
course...my brother Ryan Evans.”

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:59.139
And at the end of High School Musical 3, when
Sharpay isn’t chosen for one of the scholarships

00:07:59.139 --> 00:08:03.461
to Juilliard--even though her brother is and his stupid hat is--we learn that she’s going to help run the high

00:08:03.461 --> 00:08:08.800
school’s drama department the following
year, a role for which there will be zero glory.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.889
Sharpay is just committed to making her school’s
drama program great.

00:08:12.889 --> 00:08:17.889
She always wants to be the star, but are we
really faulting someone for wanting to be

00:08:17.889 --> 00:08:18.889
the best?

00:08:18.889 --> 00:08:22.440
A true diva wouldn’t let anyone near her
spotlight, and clearly Sharpay is still along

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:25.180
for the ride even if she isn’t getting all
the glory.

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:28.229
Complaint #2: Sharpay is trying to steal Troy
away from Gabriella.

00:08:28.229 --> 00:08:33.940
So perhaps a bigger sin of Sharpay’s is
that she has goals to date Troy who is (sometimes)

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.070
happily in a relationship with Gabriella.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:38.550
So what nefarious deed does she do to win
him over?

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:39.969
Does she kiss him?

00:08:39.969 --> 00:08:41.820
Push Gabriella off a cliff?

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:46.660
Drug him and shave off that mop of hair so
she can swim deeper into his cool blue, winter

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:48.960
crystal eyes?

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:49.460
NO!

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:55.420
Sharpay’s evil plan is to get Troy a job
at her family’s country club, get him promoted

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:59.560
so he’ll be paid better, and then also introduce him
to members of the University of Albuquerque

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.940
basketball team so that he’ll have a better
chance of getting a scholarship the following

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:03.780
year.

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:07.920
“What a shame that Troy is only washing dishes all summer given that he is a potential star for Alma Mater daddy."

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:12.000
"The Red Hawks would be very interested in him."

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.700
"Troys very concerned about college."
"Really...? How's coach Bolton these days?"

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.400
How DARE she?

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:19.480
And what insane favor does she ask of him in return?

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:21.000
That he perform with her in a talent show...

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:25.080
"She's basically offered you a college education just to sing with her in the talent show."

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:28.460
which, it probably should be mentioned when push comes to shove, he doesn’t do.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:32.920
Meanwhile, let’s look at what some of the
“good guys” do back at High School Musical

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:36.700
1: In order to get Troy and Gabriella’s
heads back into the game, their best friends

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:41.320
trick Troy into saying he doesn’t care about
Gabriella in front of a hidden camera and

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:44.040
then they force her to WATCH IT!

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:48.380
Who’s the bigger villain: the person trying
to win over a guy in a relationship by being

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:53.200
nice to him, or the people using hidden cameras
to break up their friends’ relationship

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.149
when it doesn’t serve their needs?

00:09:55.149 --> 00:09:57.149
But oh, it’s okay for them.

00:09:57.149 --> 00:09:59.089
But Sharpay’s actions are unforgiveable?

00:09:59.089 --> 00:10:01.110
Yeah... I don’t think so.

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:05.790
And complaint #3: Sharpay is a spoiled rich
girl who expects everything to be handed to

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:06.790
her.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.110
Now, the rich part is right: Throughout the
High School Musical movies, we learn that

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:13.590
Sharpay’s family owns a resort and uses
a private helicopter.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:16.060
But expecting everything to be handed to her?

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:18.430
Nothing could be further from the truth.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:22.440
In the straight-to-DVD classic, Sharpay’s
Fabulous Adventure, Sharpay moves to New York

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:26.190
City to try to make it as an actress, and
her doubting father gives her one month to

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:29.120
make a career for herself or else she’ll
have to return home.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:30.700
Does Sharpay kick and scream about it?

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:35.420
No, she actually goes and tries to make the best of it, and tries to network with a director

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:36.360
who voiced interest in casting her.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:40.240
"I'm going to meet with that casting director, get the part, be a star, and have a palace."

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:45.440
And when she finds out that director was actually
interested in casting her dog and not her,

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:50.500
sure it sucks, but she seizes the opportunity
and gets hired as the personal assistant to

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:54.790
the star of the show, who then makes her run
errands all night and scrub toilets.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:57.660
Does Sharpay refuse and resolve to destroy
the star’s career?

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:02.380
No, once again she recognizes that getting an in with
someone in the industry is how people get

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:07.480
a shot in show business, so she does all the
star’s menial chores...THEN destroys her

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:08.480
career.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:11.639
The point is, across all four installments
of the franchise, Sharpay gets knocked down

00:11:11.639 --> 00:11:17.010
time and time and time again...losing the lead
role, getting betrayed, not getting into the

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:22.190
college she wants, getting passed over for
a dog...but she never once gives up on what matters

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:24.600
to her, she never stops believing in herself,

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:28.320
"What about your dream of being a star."
"It's still there."

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.760
"It's just a little bit more of a dream than a reality."

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:33.620
and she’s even gracious enough to help others out like Gabriella

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:38.540
and this weird snooty kid with a performing King Charles Spaniel in Sharpay's Fabulous Adventure.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:43.430
By the end of the series, she gets the satisfaction
not only of coming out on top but also of

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:46.670
doing it entirely on her own.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:52.770
And that my friends the most noble, hero-esque arc we
see from anyone in the whole series.

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:56.829
Zeke had it right all along: “If you actually
get to know her…”

00:11:56.829 --> 00:12:01.290
And the heroes of these movies don’t even
let him finish talking about keeping an open

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:05.640
mind to a fellow classmate...well done Wildcats. Well done.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:08.540
"That's all well and good MatPat" you're probably saying right now.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:10.020
But HSM needs a villain...

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:11.280
So who then IS the villain?

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:16.640
Well, you’re in luck, because the series
does have someone who is truly spoiled, someone

00:12:16.649 --> 00:12:19.400
who doesn’t deserve the things they have
coming to them, and then is ungrateful for

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:21.230
the opportunities that come their way.

00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:25.420
It’s none other than the six-packed, autotuned
wonder, Troy Bolton.

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:29.350
I mean, it starts all the way back in the
first movie: When the time comes for Troy

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:34.000
and Gabriella to audition, they chicken out,
and only gather enough courage after it’s

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.000
too late.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:38.420
“We take these shows very seriously
at East High.

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:41.870
I called for the pairs audition and you didn’t
respond.

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:45.860
Free period is now over.”, but apparently
not seriously enough since Ms. Darbus hears

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:47.560
them singing and gives them a callback anyway.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:50.260
"Bolton, Montez, you have a call back."

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:53.800
And if you want to talk about someone who
won’t share the spotlight, look no further

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:58.380
than Troy Bolton in High School Musical 2, when Troy is invited to play pick-up basketball with the players

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:02.839
on the University of Albuquerque’s team,
an opportunity I should mention he only gets

00:13:02.839 --> 00:13:04.050
thanks to Sharpay.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:08.730
His friends on his high school team ask to
go and Troy doesn’t even consider it before

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:09.940
he refuses.

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:13.740
"Hey hey, Bolton, come on!"
"Hey! Why don't you tell them to come over here and mix it up?"

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:16.920
"Show em' some game."
"I don't think that's how they roll. It's a closed practice."

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:19.280
"But we can play two on two after work...?"

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:20.980
Just flat-out ditches them.

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:26.040
Speaking of being a bad friend, he breaks
pretty much every promise he makes to his girlfriend Gabriella

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:30.380
in HSM 2, then uses Sharpay’s affection
to get more money and access to people who

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:31.340
can help him out

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:35.540
"An entire table of university boosters are coming to see you... THANKS to me!"

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:39.420
"So I'll be their waiter, they'll be thrilled."
"Troy, Troy this could change your life!"

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:42.100
"I'm more interested in what my friends think of me."

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:47.900
All in return for singing a song in a talent show
with Sharpay that he acts like is a huge chore

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:49.960
the entire time and ultimately doesn't deliver on.

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:55.300
"You'll sing some other time though... With me. Promise?"
"Promise."

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:59.240
Well sorry, Mr. Swoopy Bangs, didn’t mean
to give you an opportunity to pay for the

00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:01.120
college you say you can’t afford.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:05.320
"Troy's very concerned about college."
"Really? How's coach Bolton these days?"

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:08.060
"Oh, fantastic!"
"Outstanding"

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:11.420
"Next time I see country club princess I'm gonna launch her and her pink car straight into the lake."

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:12.680
"Build the ramp buddy."

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:17.660
Speaking of that job, Troy spends most of
the movie worried about money, but then spends

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:21.140
most of his time at the job getting others to completely
ignore their duties.

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:22.660
"I'm sorry I'm late Mr. Fulton."

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:27.400
Or just slacking off with his friends: 
"Mr. Fulton this was my idea she had nothing to do with it."

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:32.720
"I generously overlooked your previous break violation, but then came the golf course incident."

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:37.080
"And now... this. Two strikes."

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.100
It’s a JOB!

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.080
You gotta do your job

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:43.600
to EARN the money. You're going to have to earn your way into that college, Troy!

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:49.519
Or maybe you don’t...because life hands
Troy Bolton whatever the eff' he wants.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:53.069
At the end of High School Musical 3, it’s
announced that Troy will attend UC Berkeley

00:14:53.069 --> 00:14:59.160
because he chooses “basketball...but I've also choosen theater”.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:14:59.940
Yeah, Troy?

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:01.839
Are they letting you play basketball at Berkeley?

00:15:01.839 --> 00:15:05.170
Who did you Coach father have to pay off to
let that one happen?

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:09.880
Because THAT’S a big time, Division I sports
school -- which, for everyone who doesn’t

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:14.100
talk sports translates to, these guys are
SERIOUS about their athletics.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:20.899
In the 2017-2018 college basketball season,
no starting player on their team is shorter

00:15:20.899 --> 00:15:23.120
than 6 foot 3.

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:25.770
Zac Efron is 5 foot 8.

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:27.200
He is shorter than me!

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:32.000
Which begs the question: How is Troy Bolton,
the theater-basketball double-threat able

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.070
to manage that?

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:35.759
Could it be because things just get handed
to him?

00:15:35.759 --> 00:15:39.629
His spot on the basketball team, his job at
the country club, and let’s not forget that

00:15:39.629 --> 00:15:43.860
he never even formally auditioned for the
show in the original High School Musical!

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:48.699
If you’re looking for somebody to hate,
maybe look away from the hard-working rich

00:15:48.699 --> 00:15:53.130
girl and look more at the popular kid who
always gets whatever he wants whether he deserves

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:54.130
it or not.

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:58.790
I guess good things come to those with abs….I’m
gonna go do some crunches.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:02.050
But hey, that’s just a theory.

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:04.769
A Film Theory! Annnnnd...

00:16:04.769 --> 00:16:08.240
You know, as hard as I tried I couldn’t
figure out how to prove that High School Musical

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:13.480
was in the same universe as Breaking Bad (even
though Gabriella is a science whiz who has

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:18.500
been moving every year and might be being
chased by the DEA or Gus Fring’s daughter

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:22.860
or something; hey, if you can make an air-tight
connection, let me know because that would be the best theory ever).

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:26.060
High School Musical is the prequel to Breaking Bad?

00:16:26.140 --> 00:16:29.580
In the meantime, hit the subscribe button to ensure you get more theories sent to your door

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:31.080
that will ruin your childhood.

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:34.540
You can bet on it, bet on it, bet on it...bet
on ME!

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:38.840
And if you want MORE Disney ruined for you,
check out how Moana and Maui are secretly

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:40.960
related...along with her pig.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.520
That’s the box to the left!

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.740
Now if you'll excuse me, I do really need to do those crunches.

